{"title":"Metamorphosis of Frogs","puid":"c-sci-5-gb/az2g6o","path":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/level-06","type":"normal","keyboardLayout":"standardNATENG","voiceLang":"en","voice":"f3_2025","instruction":{"voice":"m2_2025","speaker":true},"image":{"width":200},"lsg":{"width":300},"hint":{"speaker":true,"autoplay":false},"trainers":[{"trainer":"gapMulti","onSamePage":true,"finishButton":false,"gapMode":"buttons","instruction":{"text":"Fill in the gaps."},"soundMode":"b","textAlign":"left","shuffleButtons":true,"combineButtons":true,"removeCorrectButton":true,"hint":{"text":["This picture shows a frog’s life cycle.",{"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/lsg/frog_2.lsg","width":150}}],"label":"Frog’s Life Cycle"},"atoms":[{"b":"A <b>frog’s life cycle</b> begins with laying ((++eggs)). Some frogs can lay up to 6,000 eggs.","lsg":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/lsg/frog_6.lsg"},{"b":"The <b>second stage</b> is the larvae stage. Frog larvae are more commonly known as ((++tadpoles)). The larvae hatch from eggs, live in ((++water)) and don’t have limbs yet.","lsg":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/lsg/frog_5.lsg"},{"b":"In the <b>third stage</b>, the tadpoles grow into <b>froglets</b> and start to develop ((++limbs_and_lungs)). This transformation is important for the adult frog to be able to live on land.","lsg":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/lsg/frog_7.lsg"},{"b":"In the ((++final_stage)) of its life cycle, the frog is able to climb out of the water and live its life on ((++land)) — but always close to water. Once the adult frog lays eggs, the life cycle can begin again.","lsg":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/lsg/frog_8.lsg"}]},{"trainer":"dragMatch","instruction":{"text":"Match each photo of the <b>Northern Leopard frog’s life cycle</b> with the correct stage."},"soundMode":"a","shuffleAtoms":true,"image":{"width":120},"atoms":[{"a":{"text":"Stage&nbsp;1","sound":"stage 1"},"b":{"image":"adobe_181535901"}},{"a":{"text":"Stage&nbsp;2","sound":"stage 2"},"b":{"image":"adobe_318441048"}},{"a":{"text":"Stage&nbsp;3","sound":"stage 3"},"b":{"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/lsg/frog_4.lsg","width":120}}},{"a":{"text":"Stage&nbsp;4","sound":"stage 4"},"b":{"image":"adobe_56191392_crop-797-0-2694-2694"}}]},{"trainer":"lsg","gapMode":"buttons","soundMode":"a","instruction":{"text":"Select the correct names of the stages in the <b>Northern Leopard frog’s life cycle</b>."},"shuffleButtons":true,"combineButtons":true,"removeCorrectButton":true,"finishButton":false,"lsg":{"lsg":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/lsg/frog.cycle.lsg","width":400},"atoms":[{"id":"first","b":"((++egg))","hideClasses":["second","third","fourth"]},{"id":"second","b":"((++tadpole))","hideClasses":["third","fourth"]},{"id":"third","b":"((++froglet))","hideClasses":["fourth"]},{"id":"fourth","b":"((++adult))"}]},{"trainer":"buttons","instruction":{"text":"True or false? Select the correct answer."},"trueFalseMode":true,"shuffleAtoms":true,"soundMode":"a","atoms":[{"a":"The Northern Leopard frog undergoes metamorphosis.","b":true,"image":"adobe_34001054"},{"a":"A frog’s body changes a lot while it grows into adulthood.","b":true,"image":"adobe_37739241_crop-222-504-3528-3528"},{"a":"As frogs grow into adulthood, they begin to grow a long tail.","b":false,"image":"adobe_60253562_crop-994-0-2999-2999"},{"a":"Frogs spend their whole life in water.","b":false,"image":"adobe_395426358"},{"a":"Frogs are amphibians.","b":true,"image":"adobe_411061336"}]}],"parentTopic":{"title":"Living Things and their Habitats","path":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/topic","puid":"c-sci-5-gb/x0pa85"},"parentBlock":{"title":"Metamorphosis","path":"/../c-sci-5-gb/topic-01-living-things-and-their-habitats/block-03-metamorphosis/block","puid":"c-sci-5-gb/wsljvz"},"mediaFiles":{"sounds":[{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/A frog’s body changes a lot while it grows into adulthood.","etag":"aed1-22076"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/A frog’s life cycle begins with laying eggs. Some frogs can lay up to 6,000 eggs.","etag":"d0f7-33452"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/As frogs grow into adulthood, they begin to grow a long tail.","etag":"5ba6-24525"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Frogs are amphibians.","etag":"f797-9981"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/Frogs spend their whole life in water.","etag":"7e34-15165"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/In the final stage of its life cycle, the frog is able to climb out of the water and live its life on land — but always close to water. Once the adult frog lays eggs, the life cycle can begin again.","etag":"a838-74061"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/In the third stage, the tadpoles grow into froglets and start to develop limbs and lungs. This transformation is important for the adult frog to be able to live on land.","etag":"476e-61533"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The Northern Leopard frog undergoes metamorphosis.","etag":"fc5c-17901"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/The second stage is the larvae stage. Frog larvae are more commonly known as tadpoles. The larvae hatch from eggs, live in water and don’t have limbs yet.","etag":"7755-59372"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/This picture shows a frog’s life cycle.","etag":"c362-15164"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/stage 1","etag":"a575-6093"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/stage 2","etag":"7909-6957"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/stage 3","etag":"99ac-6669"},{"fileId":"sound/en/f3_2025/stage 4","etag":"cbf3-6669"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Fill in the gaps.","etag":"7a75-11520"},{"fileId":"sound/en/m2_2025/Match each photo of the <b>Northern Leopard frog’s life cycle</b> with th